{"id": "1.2-00029", "case_id": "github_wangxuan95_uart2axi4_direct_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "github/wangxuan95/fpga-uart", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00029&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (5 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: RTL/uart2axi4.v, RTL/uart_rx.v, RTL/uart_tx.v. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00029&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>3 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00029&amp;file=private%2Freference%2FRTL%2Fuart2axi4.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed frozen testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>2 frozen testpoints:</strong> uart2axi4, uart_increment. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00029&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00029&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># UART command to AXI4 project\nImplement the three-module uart2axi4 project using the unchanged bilingual original README in specification/project.md. The Chinese section 3.5 contains the complete original ASCII command grammar; both language sections are part of the input. The original document covers UART streams, buffering, byte ordering, framing and command/response behavior.\n\nCurator clarification of the pinned configuration and documentation defects:\n- uart2axi4 instantiates uart_rx and uart_tx; implement all three declared files. Clock edges are rising, reset rstn is asynchronous active-low and must be asserted initially. Standalone UART defaults remain available. Qualified whole-project configuration uses CLK_FREQ=16000000, BAUD_RATE=115200, PARITY=&quot;NONE&quot;, BYTE_WIDTH=4 and A_WIDTH=32. The second upstream bench uses 4 MHz TX / 5 MHz RX, 115200 baud, odd parity, one stop bit, a two-byte TX stream with FIFO_EA=0, and RX FIFO_EA=1.\n- UART transmits start-low, eight bits LSB first, the selected parity, then STOP_BITS high stop bits. Fractional division distributes clock periods as described by the original manual. TX transmits enabled bytes least-significant byte first. All i_tkeep bits are active-high; the Chinese sentence saying i_tkeep[0]=0 selects a byte is a typo (the English section is correct). With no RX FIFO, valid is a one-cycle arrival pulse and cannot wait for ready; with buffering, unread data is held and a full queue drops a new byte, pulsing overflow.\n- Commands accept either letter case for W/R and hexadecimal digits. Spaces separate words. CR or LF terminates a command; ignored leading whitespace/empty newline does not create an operation. W&lt;address&gt; &lt;data&gt;... issues one write burst; R&lt;address&gt; &lt;length&gt; issues one read burst. Use the documented legal range 1..256 words, address/data widths from the declaration, and no commands overlapping an in-progress transaction. AXI LEN is the number of beats minus one. Write data is ordered exactly as the command; LAST accompanies its final beat. Address and data valid/ready handshakes determine acceptance. BREADY is permanently high. Read ends on the requested beat count or RLAST, whichever arrives first. No WSTRB, IDs or response-status ports exist in this simplified interface.\n- For BYTE_WIDTH=4, successful writes return the eight-character word &quot;okay    &quot;, followed by an extra space and LF; invalid commands return &quot;invalid &quot;, followed by an extra space and LF. Read data is lowercase fixed-width hexadecimal, eight characters per word, separated by spaces; a trailing space precedes the final LF. Other documented BYTE_WIDTH values truncate/pad these fixed little-endian response words to 2*BYTE_WIDTH characters. Exact response formatting is a curator clarification of the original prose&#x27;s okay/invalid examples.\n- The public contract requires initial reset. Reference-only initial assignments duplicating reset values and the parameter diagnostic printing section are removed; every original file is retained. No functional state transition or data equation is changed. This case excludes malformed numeric overflow and traffic exceeding UART reply-buffer capacity, whose behavior is not fully specified upstream.\n\nScoring uses both original benches, with explicit failure assertions, response checks and added observation of public AXI address/data ports. One bench is one point; configurations and vectors do not increase the case count. Finite verification is not exhaustive protocol proof.\n\nImplement every required path in output_contract.json. Declaration-only ports\nare in interfaces/modules.v. No initial/final, delays, simulation system tasks,\nforce/release or external includes are permitted. Only declared RTL is collected.\nMissing files, forbidden constructs or failed top compilation score zero. Each\nprivate point has equal weight and requires all of its checks to pass. Use\nterminal/file_editor, iverilog, vvp and Python iteratively; finish by saving RTL.\nRun `python3 checks/check.py` for public compilation feedback.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/7b9949ec5bc1a0e0533e75bb66fabee43da6c36f69df7175da8d5806c2f0298b.txt"